CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260430T155526Z
DESCRIPTION:Clara Rottsolk sings a collection of Broadside Ballads and Art
 s Songs from Colonial America\, newly arranged for soprano and piano trio
 \, as well as The Congress\, an original work for the same ensemble by Bi
 ll Robinson based upon a counter-revolutionary text by Rev. Jonathan Odel
 l from 1776. The program continues with two piano trios from the 20th cen
 tury: Amy Beach's romantic/impressionistic work form 1938 and Cafe Music\
 , Paul Schoenfeld's boundary crossing classic from 1987. This concert is 
 part of Duke University's "We the People" initiative\, marking the 250th 
 anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence.\n\nPROGRAM
 \nBroadside Ballads and Art Songs from Colonial Times by John Hewitt\, Fr
 ances Hopkinson\, Christian Latrobe and Mary Ann Wrighten Pownall arrange
 d for soprano and piano trio by Bill Robinson\; Robinson: The Congress\; 
 Amy Beach: Piano Trio\, Op. 150\; Paul Schoenfeld: Piano Trio Cafe Music\
 n\nARTISTS\nEric Pritchard\, violin\nClara Rottsolk\, soprano\nElizabeth 
 Anderson\, cello\nBrandt Fredriksen\, piano
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260511T143129Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260522T190000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260511T143129Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=18832edc-1b23ba5b-011b-27d4ee03-0000000e:Baldwin A
 uditorium
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Union Forever: Ideas of America (Presented by Eric Pritchard\,
  violin)
