CREATED:20260511T163956Z
DESCRIPTION:Get inspired by the next generation of innovators!\n\nWe invit
 e you to experience the creativity\, passion\, and brilliance of our stud
 ents at the Innovation for Humanity Expo Challenge\, a one-of-a-kind even
 t hosted by Durham Public Schools and designed by student innovators them
 selves.\n\nJoin us on Saturday\, May 23\, from 8 a.m. to 1:30 p.m. at the
  Duke Pratt School of Engineering for a powerful showcase of middle schoo
 l talent in action. Students from Rogers-Herr\, Githens\, Brogden\, and N
 eal middle schools will present original ideas and solutions tackling rea
 l-world challenges\, demonstrating the impact of innovation\, collaborati
 on\, and forward-thinking in education.\n\nThis year's Expo will also hig
 hlight the incredible leadership behind the work. At Rogers-Herr\, the Ra
 m Innovators are guided by Tabetha Evans\, who was recently named her sch
 ool's Beginning Teacher of the Year and is a finalist for the district Be
 ginning Teacher of the Year.\n\nCome see what's possible when students ar
 e empowered to lead\, create\, and solve. You won't want to miss it.\n\nT
 he event is free and open to the community.
DURATION:PT5H30M
DTSTAMP:20260511T163956Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260523T080000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260511T163956Z
