DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special one‑day symposium\, celebrating two majo
 r milestones in Duke's research legacy: 30 years of clinical research exc
 ellence from the Duke Clinical Research Institute (DCRI) and 20 years of 
 innovating research translation from the Clinical and Translational Scien
 ce Award (CTSA) at Duke. We are honored to feature Dr. Robert M. Califf a
 s a keynote speaker. Dr. Califf is the founding director of DCRI\, PI of 
 our first CTSA\, former U.S. FDA Commissioner\, and a globally recognized
  leader in clinical research\, health outcomes\, and translational scienc
 e. The symposium features a morning of plenary sessions\, panels\, and sh
 ort talks\, networking lunch\, and an afternoon of concurrent sessions an
 d interactive workshops highlighting collaboration\, trust\, and real‑wor
 ld impact. Open to all Duke\, NCCU\, and Durham Tech faculty\, staff\, an
 d students\, as well as community collaborators and partners. Agenda and 
 Registration at https://ctsi.duke.edu/trustworthy-translation
DURATION:PT6H
